  "notes": "West leads the ♣10 against 3♠. West's club lead is won in dummy. South must avoid the loss of 3 diamond tricks and 2 trump tricks.\n\nIf South crosses in hearts and plays a diamond to the ♦K and ♦A, East will return a trump. If East has the ♦Q, South will have to guess the trump position to make the contract.\n\nSouth can make the contract without guessing by leading the ♦4 from dummy at trick 2. If East has the ♦Q, South will have held his diamond losers to 2. He can afford to lose 2 trump tricks if necessary.\n\nIf West has the ♦Q, he cannot afford to play trump from his side of the table without holding South's trump losers to 1. If West has all 4 trumps he can exit with a low trump. South plays a second round of diamonds. If West has the ♦A, he will not be able to prevent a diamond ruff except by surrendering 1 of his trump tricks.\n\nUpon winning the ♦Q, West will exit passively. A diamond is played. For South to have any problem, East must win the ♦A and return a trump. South can either finesse or win the ♠A and be certain of making the contract.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♣10 against 3♠. West's club lead is won in dummy. South must avoid the loss of 3 diamond tricks and 2 trump tricks.",
    "If South crosses in hearts and plays a diamond to the ♦K and ♦A, East will return a trump. If East has the ♦Q, South will have to guess the trump position to make the contract.",
    "South can make the contract without guessing by leading the ♦4 from dummy at trick 2. If East has the ♦Q, South will have held his diamond losers to 2. He can afford to lose 2 trump tricks if necessary.",
    "If West has the ♦Q, he cannot afford to play trump from his side of the table without holding South's trump losers to 1. If West has all 4 trumps he can exit with a low trump. South plays a second round of diamonds. If West has the ♦A, he will not be able to prevent a diamond ruff except by surrendering 1 of his trump tricks.",
    "Upon winning the ♦Q, West will exit passively. A diamond is played. For South to have any problem, East must win the ♦A and return a trump. South can either finesse or win the ♠A and be certain of making the contract."
